---
title: 'v01.0: Give every command one error envelope'
description: Replace bare thrown strings with a typed error the CLI renders once
---

# v01.0: Give every command one error envelope

Each command throws a bare `Error` with a prefixed message, so the CLI has no way to tell a usage failure from a runtime one and every command spells the prefix itself.

- [ ] Outcome: a typed error carries a code and a message, and the CLI renders it in one place
- [ ] Outcome: no command constructs its own error prefix
